---
title: "try_map_referral_code (protocol::referral)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_bound: self, user, maybe_referral
    q_check_bound --> q_return_existing: self.referee_to_code.contains(user)
    q_check_bound --> q_check_none: !self.referee_to_code.contains(user)
    q_return_existing --> [*]: return some(*self.referee_to_code.borrow(user))
    q_check_none --> q_return_none: maybe_referral.is_none()
    q_check_none --> q_extract: !maybe_referral.is_none()
    q_return_none --> [*]: return maybe_referral (none)
    q_extract --> q_validate_code: code = *maybe_referral.borrow()
    q_validate_code --> q_error_invalid: !self.code_owner.contains(code)
    q_validate_code --> q_check_self_ref: self.code_owner.contains(code)
    q_error_invalid --> [*]: abort referral_invalid_referral_code()
    q_check_self_ref --> q_error_self: owner == user
    q_check_self_ref --> q_bind: owner != user
    q_error_self --> [*]: abort referral_no_self_reference()
    q_bind --> [*]: self.referee_to_code.add(user, code), return maybe_referral

    note right of q_check_bound
        INV-001: Once bound, a referee-to-code mapping is permanent and never changes
        INV-002: A user cannot use their own referral code (no self-reference)
        INV-003: The referral code must exist in code_owner table
        INV-004: If user already bound, returns existing code regardless of maybe_referral
    end note
